{
  "_": [
    "THE DIRECTION FOR 'The City That Learned To Watch'.",
    "",
    "Two instruments, and only two, because they are the two the system",
    "actually has: a CURVE that moves across the acts, and PROSE direction",
    "on the beats that need more than the curve.",
    "",
    "Nothing here names a primitive, a colour or an effect. 'ordinary and",
    "indifferent' is a register the compiler reads; what it builds from it",
    "is the compiler's business. That is the whole test of whether there is",
    "a director model — if this file had to say `pixel_quantise` it would",
    "be an effects list with a nicer name.",
    "",
    "THE ARC, which is the reason a 38-scene film is not 38 unrelated",
    "pictures:",
    "",
    "  I    the physical city. Concrete, archival, people in it, held still.",
    "  II   the fragments connect. Data rises, the human falls away, the",
    "       picture climbs off the literal.",
    "  III  accumulation. The densest and most POPULATED act in the film —",
    "       'thousands of ordinary decisions' has to be a world with too",
    "       much in it, not a caption reading THOUSANDS.",
    "  IV   the system, seen plainly. Most abstract, least human, most",
    "       data. Nothing hidden and nothing warm.",
    "  V    the same street. Returns close to Act I and deliberately NOT to",
    "       it — a shade more abstract, a shade less archival. 'Only the",
    "       meaning of the walk has changed' is a claim about the viewer,",
    "       so the picture must be almost the same and not quite."
  ],
